{"kind":"request","text":"Repair the documentation reading paths found by the 10 November review\n\nHugh asked on 10 November 2026 whether the documentation gives each audience a coherent path. Five reviewers walked main 8289d9e5 as a newcomer and room member, an application author, an agent connector, an operator, and a security reviewer and contributor. The link checker passes with 1,098 links. The two tutorials run exactly as written from the published packages. Three audiences have no working path, and feature heads since 1 November added project run records to reader pages. The five reports, with line numbers, are in /Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-10-docs-path-review/.\n\nWork, in order.\n\nA. Correct the errors of fact.\n1. roadmap.md:81 says OAuth on the hosted endpoint is not built. packages/mcp/src/oauth-*.ts and mcp.md:1954 show it is.\n2. deploy.md:177 says unqualified installs keep register 18. NEWEST is register 26.\n3. deploy.md:151-154 and 192-195 contradict INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES at 297 and 468.\n4. operations.md:8 says the room template declares METRICS. apps/room/wrangler.jsonc does not.\n5. scopes.md:19 counts twelve packages and omits dap-define.\n6. first-change.md:62 says there is no `dap propose` and no browser editor. Both exist.\n7. o4-connect.md:160 and 182 name a tool `open_issue`. The tool is `issue.create`.\n8. homepage/src/room/index.html sends \"Open room\" to artroom-scope, which creates no room.\n9. apps/room/README.md:14 and celld.md:8 name artroom-scope as the template's Worker. It is dap-self-host.\n10. Node version: self-host.md and celld.md say 26, cli.md says 22.0.0, the tutorials say 22.18, package.json says 22. State one.\n11. cli.md:732 omits `establish-application` from the acts that take `--value`.\n12. skills/dap-application links to the repository's old name and calls dap-define a spike.\n\nB. Give each reader a start.\n1. Rebuild docs/README.md and the root README around what the reader wants to do: take part in a room, connect an AI app, build an application, run a service, check the security, contribute. The homepage links follow.\n2. Rewrite apps/room/docs (first-change, reviewing, landing, roles-and-membership, page) as current guides. They are 9 to 14 October drafts with status paragraphs and \"manual outcome\" ledgers. Add the browser path and \"file an issue\". Use one name for a change version.\n3. Add \"Get the dap command\" (clone, npm ci, alias) until the CLI is published.\n4. Add \"Connect an AI app to a room\" for a Claude or ChatGPT user, with a line that names the hosts that work today.\n5. Add \"Contribute to dap\": setup, where code lives, one test, the gate, review. Replace contribute.md.\n6. Add \"Operate a service\": upgrade, rollback, backup, secret rotation, retire a Worker, read logs.\n\nC. Split the pages that serve several readers.\n1. mcp.md: keep lines 1-1847 (the test-bound agent reference). Move the hosted endpoint and metrics to a new operator page. Move the budget figures to notes/.\n2. testing.md: keep the daily how-to (about 200 lines). Move stand-ins and gate internals to a reference page, and evidence filing to a workroom-process page.\n3. self-host.md: one Cloudflare page and one Mac page. Move the register text at 8-27 to the operator page.\n4. deploy.md: open with \"The order\". Move the section that follows \"## Source\" above it.\n5. write-an-application.md: keep the how-to and teach it with the tutorial applications. Move package composition and device commands to a package reference. Say that dap-define is checkout-only and needs tsx.\n6. application-views.md: add \"A minimal view\" first.\n7. Add \"Check and preview a package\": `dap new`, `dap check`, a refusal scenario, `dap dev`.\n\nD. Move the project's own records out of reader pages.\no4-connect.md, self-host.md:454-617, the Commons and artroom-scope sections of deploy.md, the opening run status of the lending and grow runbooks, apps/room/docs/ledger.md, and each \"the planner\" and ruling ID in docs/security. State each rule without its ruling.\n\nE. Security index.\nOne ordered list in SECURITY.md and docs/README.md: threat model, trust boundaries, definition authors, entry points, settings, contracts. Retitle threat-model.md \"Threat model\" and open it with what is protected, from whom, and what is assumed.\n\nF. Say plainly what does not work yet, on the page where the reader meets it.\nNo new room installs an ordinary package (run-your-app.md:11, self-host.md:180). Refresh the \"Checked against\" footers, and link notes/README.md from the index as the design history.\n\nItems B3, B4, B6 and F change again when the wind-down work lands the published CLI, package install in a new room, the hosted connector acceptance and the deploy runbook. Write them for today and revise them with those heads.","body":{"conditions":"Each lettered group lands on main as documents with the link checker and the document-bound tests passing; a reader page names no planner, builder, checker or ruling ID.","target_head":"8289d9e5303183606544a2b086174cd0ed2154b2","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}